WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.012 --> 00:00:06.296
Early the next morning, the computer whirred to life.

2
00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:07.537
"Wake up.

3
00:00:07.617 --> 00:00:10.379
Time to report to work."

4
00:00:10.399 --> 00:00:32.449
"I'm not going," Ally and yanked the covers over her head.

5
00:00:32.469 --> 00:00:35.551
"Irrational reply," the computer said.

6
00:00:35.571 --> 00:00:38.872
"Need fuel and new parts for travel to Astralia."

7
00:00:39.713 --> 00:00:41.674
"I can't go back to the diner.

8
00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:45.096
Mateo hates me," Ally said.

9
00:00:45.116 --> 00:00:49.018
"Irrational reply," the computer repeated.

10
00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:51.739
"An Astralian never gives up on a mission."

11
00:00:51.759 --> 00:00:59.704
"Fine!" Ally got up and threw on her meld medallion.

12
00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:04.320
"I'll go find another job!

13
00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:05.261
Are you happy?"

14
00:01:05.281 --> 00:01:08.462
"Irrational question," the computer replied.

15
00:01:12.323 --> 00:01:15.264
Ally left the park and walked into town to look for a new job.

16
00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:22.306
But in order to get to some of the other businesses, she had to walk past Ray's.

17
00:01:22.326 --> 00:01:24.746
"I'll just run," she thought.

18
00:01:25.247 --> 00:01:29.248
Then, as she got closer to the diner, she spotted Ray and Mateo out front.

19
00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.125
She ducked into a nearby alley.

20
00:01:33.145 --> 00:01:37.108
"Mateo, I insist," Ray said.

21
00:01:37.128 --> 00:01:39.189
"You must go to camp today.

22
00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:42.171
The last few months have been hard enough on our family.

23
00:01:42.832 --> 00:01:44.173
I want you to have some fun."

24
00:01:44.193 --> 00:01:46.894
"I don't want you to be lonely, Papi.

25
00:01:47.395 --> 00:01:51.257
Besides, if Ally has quit, it's all my fault."

26
00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:57.902
"I doubt you're the reason she didn't show up today," Ray said.

27
00:01:57.922 --> 00:02:01.064
"With so few customers, she couldn't make enough money here.

28
00:02:01.936 --> 00:02:03.837
I'm sure she found a better-paying job."

29
00:02:05.198 --> 00:02:06.038
Mateo sighed.

30
00:02:06.058 --> 00:02:08.739
"I shouldn't have yelled at her.

31
00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:12.421
Especially since I finally got up the nerve to text Bethany.

32
00:02:12.861 --> 00:02:18.384
Because of Ally, I invited Bethany to the sci-fi convention at the UFO museum next week, and she

33
00:02:18.444 --> 00:02:19.144
said yes!"

34
00:02:19.164 --> 00:02:22.086
"That's great, son."

35
00:02:23.006 --> 00:02:26.168
Ray wrapped an arm around Mateo's shoulder and led him back inside.

36
00:02:32.604 --> 00:02:34.125
Ally ran a hand through her hair.

37
00:02:34.145 --> 00:02:37.426
"Mateo's not mad at me anymore," she thought.

38
00:02:37.446 --> 00:02:39.387
"And Ray needs my help.

39
00:02:40.207 --> 00:02:46.290
Maybe A minute later she strolled into the diner as if nothing had ever happened.

40
00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:50.172
"I'm sorry I'm late, I—" "You're back," Ray said.

41
00:02:50.192 --> 00:02:54.734
"I'm sorry I yelled at you, Ally," Mateo said.

42
00:02:54.754 --> 00:02:57.915
"I was just embarrassed in front of Bethany."

43
00:02:59.175 --> 00:03:00.096
Ally waved her hand.

44
00:03:00.804 --> 00:03:02.485
"I've already forgotten about it.

45
00:03:03.586 --> 00:03:05.988
Don't you have a camp to get to, Mateo?"

46
00:03:06.008 --> 00:03:07.750
"Yes," he said.

47
00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:24.944
"And thanks to you, I've also got a date with Later in the day, customers began to trickle

48
00:03:25.024 --> 00:03:29.848
in. There was a family of four who ordered burgers, fries, and milkshakes.

49
00:03:33.272 --> 00:03:37.956
There was also a woman with bright red hair, rhinestone glasses, and a leopard-print dress.

50
00:03:39.437 --> 00:03:40.558
Phil came running in.

51
00:03:40.578 --> 00:03:44.441
"Just a coffee to go.

52
00:03:44.822 --> 00:03:46.163
I've got to get back to the museum.

53
00:03:46.923 --> 00:03:49.866
There's a big alien-hunting crowd over there today."

54
00:03:49.886 --> 00:03:53.729
"What?" Ally's stomach turned to knots.

55
00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:57.512
She tried to read Phil's mind, but all she could see was a doughnut.

56
00:03:57.532 --> 00:04:03.104
"You know, a huge tour group," Phil said.

57
00:04:03.124 --> 00:04:08.628
"They come to the museum thinking they'll find proof of aliens and UFOs and try to track them

58
00:04:08.688 --> 00:04:10.669
down. Can you imagine?"

59
00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.371
Ally gave a little laugh.

60
00:04:12.391 --> 00:04:18.735
"Nope!" Then she handed Phil his coffee and a doughnut.

61
00:04:18.755 --> 00:04:20.676
"Here, it's on the house."

62
00:04:20.696 --> 00:04:25.399
"Chocolate! My favorite.

63
00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:26.300
How'd you know?"

64
00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:27.321
Phil asked.

65
00:04:28.241 --> 00:04:28.742
She shrugged.

66
00:04:28.762 --> 00:04:30.343
"Lucky guess."

67
00:04:36.156 --> 00:04:39.417
Ally put some of her tip money in the cash register to pay for Phil's doughnut.

68
00:04:42.359 --> 00:04:45.060
Then she went to serve the woman in the leopard-print dress.

69
00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:47.161
"Do you know what you'd like?"

70
00:04:48.441 --> 00:04:49.362
"I wish I did."

71
00:04:50.342 --> 00:04:51.603
The woman stared at the menu.

72
00:04:51.623 --> 00:04:54.464
"Let's see if I can help," Ally said.

73
00:04:55.024 --> 00:04:59.086
She quickly scanned the woman's thoughts and saw a plate of eggs with spicy salsa.

74
00:04:59.106 --> 00:05:03.868
"How about Ray's huevos rancheros?

75
00:05:04.852 --> 00:05:09.014
That's two fried eggs on a crispy tortilla, salsa, and cheese."

76
00:05:09.935 --> 00:05:11.096
The woman's face lit up.

77
00:05:11.116 --> 00:05:14.177
"That's exactly what I've been craving.

78
00:05:14.197 --> 00:05:18.540
I didn't see it on the menu, but you read my mind!"

79
00:05:24.963 --> 00:05:29.005
Ten minutes later Ally was crossing the dining room with the woman's order and trying not to think

80
00:05:29.045 --> 00:05:30.066
about what Phil had said.

81
00:05:30.586 --> 00:05:33.508
It sounded like some humans actually hunted for aliens.

82
00:05:34.332 --> 00:05:37.233
"I'm in more danger than I realized," Ally thought.

83
00:05:37.914 --> 00:05:39.454
She hadn't been looking where she was going.

84
00:05:39.474 --> 00:05:41.395
"Maybe I'd better—oops!"

85
00:05:41.735 --> 00:05:45.076
As Ally slammed into an empty table, the plate of eggs flew up into the air.

86
00:05:45.637 --> 00:05:48.258
Instinctively Ally activated her levitating ability.

87
00:05:48.678 --> 00:05:50.359
The plate froze, floating in midair.

88
00:05:50.379 --> 00:05:52.639
"Ack!" she thought.

89
00:05:52.659 --> 00:05:54.360
"I shouldn't have done that!"

90
00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:58.422
Ally quickly grabbed the plate and looked around to see if anyone had spotted her trick.

91
00:05:59.282 --> 00:06:01.803
The woman in the leopard-print dress was looking right at her.

92
00:06:02.603 --> 00:06:05.173
When Ally met her eyes, the woman quickly looked away.
